correspondence_templates.body:
Dear {{ applicant_name }},

Your Skilled Worker visa application has been successful.

Application reference: {{ case_reference }}
Decision date: {{ decision_date }}
Application track: {{ application_track }}
Sponsor: {{ sponsor_name }}
Occupation code: {{ occupation_code }}
Approved salary considered: {{ approved_salary }}
Permission start date: {{ grant_start_date }}
Permission end date: {{ grant_end_date }}

We are satisfied that you meet the relevant requirements for this route, including sponsorship, eligible occupation, salary and English language requirements, and any additional evidence requirements that apply in your case.

Relevant policy references: SW-SPONSOR-01, SW-SPONSOR-02, SW-JOB-01, SW-SALARY-01, SW-ENGLISH-01, SW-DECISION-01.

You must continue to comply with the conditions of your permission. If you change employer or move to a role with a different occupation code, you may need to make a new Skilled Worker application to update your permission. Overtime in your sponsored job is not limited, but separate work or self-employment is limited to 20 hours a week where permitted by the route information available in this case type.

If this decision also covers a dependant application, the dependant permission will usually end on the same date as the main applicant's permission.

Yours sincerely,
UK Visas and Immigration
Home Office
